[00:00.0 --> 00:10.0]
Now the teammate's side. A different rysh session -- think different machine. No spec file here, no credentials, nothing running on port eighty-ninety-nine.

[00:10.0 --> 00:28.0]
List what the team shares... there's the billing API. One subscribe -- and MY agent now has YOUR localhost API as a set of tools.

[00:28.0 --> 01:25.0]
Ask the agent for this month's unpaid invoices. It picks the billing tools, the call tunnels to the owner's machine, executes there, and the answer comes back -- live data from an API this machine could never reach directly.

[01:25.0 --> 02:05.0]
Now try to void one. The agent confirms -- then the owner's policy answers: mutating operations are denied by default. The owner decides which writes are ever allowed, and the server enforces it. Paranoid defaults, on purpose.

[02:05.0 --> 02:12.0]
Expose your internal API to agents -- not to the internet. rysh, at rysh-dot-A-I -- onboarding design partners now.

